{
 "about": "3-D FDTD ringdowns of a dielectric puck on an infinite ground plane, HE11 mode, from otahub.num.dra.cylinder. aspect = a/h; k0a = k0*radius at resonance; Q = Re/(2 Im). Air margin 14 cells, CPML 12, float32. 'train' made the cylindrical_dra fits; 'test' was held out (other permittivities and aspects, and three points re-run on a grid half as fine again). 'outside' holds the flat pucks beyond a/h = 4, which the fits do not cover. At eps_r 12 and below their HE11 mode has Q under 2, gone before the ringdown window opens, and the solver reports a higher mode instead; at eps_r 15 and above the ringdowns are sound, but the fit domain was kept rectangular. Kept so that the limit is on record, not fitted.",
